     1	# Circuit images in chat, with optional exploration
     2	
     3	The `circuitkit-mcp` executable serves two read-only tools over stdio:
     4	
     5	- `show_circuit` is the default. It returns a PNG and structured connectivity.
     6	  It has no UI template, even when the client supports MCP Apps. Explanations
     7	  and revision requests stay in the conversation.
     8	- `explore_circuit` opens a separate interactive viewer when explicitly requested.
     9	  It offers selection on the drawing, zoom and authored teaching scenes. Hosts
    10	  without the MCP Apps HTML capability receive a PNG fallback.
    11	
    12	Both tools use the existing CircuitKit renderers and validators. CircuitKit does
    13	not simulate electricity. The source revision includes the executable; these
    14	instructions do not imply a new registry release.
    15	
    16	## Run locally
    17	
    18	```sh
    19	bun install --frozen-lockfile
    20	bun run build
    21	node dist/mcp/cli.js --help
    22	codex mcp add circuitkit -- node "$PWD/dist/mcp/cli.js"
    23	```
    24	
    25	Registration stores the absolute checkout path. Keep that checkout and its
    26	installed dependencies available. Reload the client's MCP servers or start a new
    27	session if the tools do not appear. Tool discovery does not establish interactive
    28	UI support; that capability belongs to the chat host.
    29	
    30	## Input and output
    31	
    32	Both tools accept one optional input. Omit all inputs for the existing RC filter.
    33	
    34	```json
    35	{"recipe":"rc-lowpass"}
    36	```
    37	
    38	```json
    39	{"source":"circuit sensor v1\ntitle \"Sensor signals\"\nview wiring\nController: controller (SDA SCL)\nSensor: sensor (SDA SCL)\nController.SDA <-> Sensor.SDA\nController.SCL -> Sensor.SCL\n"}
    40	```
    41	
    42	`document` accepts a CircuitKit recipe document, including component values,
    43	presentation highlights and teaching steps. To revise an image, call `show_circuit`
    44	again with the updated document or source. All nine recipe IDs are supported.
    45	Inputs are bounded to 64 KiB and treated as inert data. Filesystem paths and
    46	executable author code are not accepted.
    47	
    48	Successful `show_circuit` calls contain one PNG image block and no widget payload.
    49	`structuredContent` gives the circuit identity, components/modules, declared nets,
    50	scenes, selected presentation mode and negotiated UI capability. Invalid input or
    51	failed PNG rendering returns `isError` without a stale image or circuit payload.
    52	
    53	Only `explore_circuit` advertises the resource `ui://circuitkit/view-v1.html`, with
    54	MIME type `text/html;profile=mcp-app`. It uses the official MCP Apps SDK 2.0 and
    55	standard `_meta.ui.resourceUri` metadata, plus the ChatGPT `openai/outputTemplate`
    56	alias. Its `_meta.circuitkit` result carries the viewer input. The self-contained
    57	HTML declares empty external connection and resource allowlists and requests no
    58	host border. `uiAdvertised` records negotiation, not proof of display.
    59	
    60	## Optional viewer
    61	
    62	The drawing is the primary surface. Components and source modules are selectable
    63	on their symbols; recipe nets are selectable on the wires or with keyboard focus
    64	and Enter. Escape clears selection. Zoom and authored scene controls sit below
    65	the drawing. The explanation action appears only after a selection and is disabled
    66	if the host does not support messages.
    67	
    68	Selections use `ui/update-model-context`. **Explain selection** explicitly sends
    69	`ui/message` with the circuit identity and target. Rejected requests are shown in
    70	the viewer. New inputs, cancellation and invalid results clear its current context.
    71	Source scenes can play illustrative flows; reduced motion removes the moving
    72	sweep and hidden documents pause it. Host theme changes affect the controls while
    73	preserving authored circuit colors.
    74	
    75	## Verify locally
    76	
    77	```sh
    78	bun run build:mcp
    79	bun test tests/mcp.test.ts
    80	bun scripts/preview-mcp.ts
    81	```
    82	
    83	The loopback preview starts with the actual PNG returned by `show_circuit`.
    84	**Explore circuit** calls the other tool and mounts its HTML through the official
    85	`AppBridge` in an iframe with `sandbox="allow-scripts"` and a network-blocking CSP.
    86	Host diagnostics are collapsed by default. This reference host records messages;
    87	it does not generate an assistant reply or establish native chat UI support.
    88	
    89	```sh
    90	bun scripts/check-mcp-browser.ts http://127.0.0.1:PORT/
    91	```
    92	
    93	The `agent-browser` check covers image output, optional exploration, pointer and
    94	keyboard selection, scenes, zoom, messages, missing host capabilities, rejected
    95	requests, cancellation, recovery, theme, mobile controls and reduced motion.
    96	Screenshots and command receipts go to `artifacts/mcp-apps/browser` by default.
    97	
    98	Set `CIRCUITKIT_MCP_AUDIT` to an absolute JSONL path for optional client capability,
    99	resource-read and tool-identity logs. It does not log circuit source or write to
   100	protocol stdout.
   101	
   102	References:
   103	
   104	- [MCP Apps specification and SDK](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps)
   105	- [OpenAI MCP and UI quickstart](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/app-quickstart/)

